    "doc": "JRPL_JRPH_series.pdf",
    "page": "4 to 7",
    "section": "JRPL Series ordering schematic"
  },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the JRPL ordering schematic, which the combined JRPL/JRPH sheet prints twice, both printings agreeing. Piston operated, so the diaphragm position carries the sheet's single 00 None code. Range springs are colour coded on the sheet, silver, beige, purple and black, kept in the labels. The PDF was read on 26 July 2026 and settles the JRPH question: there is no JRPH ordering schematic. Pages 5 to 6 and 7 to 8 both print this same JRPL schematic, headed JRPL SERIES ORDERING SCHEMATIC on all four, with only the footer of the second printing marked JRPH/0120. The JRPH's own specification page lists different spring ranges by colour alone, black 0-2150, orange 0-4060 and green 0-5800, none of which appear in the range spring table printed here, which stops at 1160 psi. So a JRPH cannot be ordered from this document and no JRPH model is built; how LowFlow codes its springs is a question for them. The gauge-span liability note is encoded as cautions, stated plainly and never blocking.",
